Flutter is basically a widget inside a widget
    - Widgets are capitalized
    - arguments are lower cased
    - to put a widget inside another widget, you need to use an argument


You must have a build method! Defined on every widget and 
will always return another widget

Stateful widgets:
when a widget's apperance or data needs to change during its lifetime
    - you also ened a companion state object
    - the stateful widget itself is immutable
    - the state object is mutable -> UI updates
        - when you mutate state obkect
            - call setState to signal framework to update the UI and call build method again

Implicit aniamtions: groups of widgets that automatically animate changes to their properties without you needing to manage any intermediate behavior
    - AnimatedContainer

Use const when the value is known at compile time and will never change
    - const pi = 3.14159
    - using const lets Flutter reuse widgets isntead of rebuilding them

Use final when the value is assigned once at runtime
    - you cannot reassign them later

Use var when the variable with change
    - var score = 0;
    - score++;
    - var message = "Hi!";
    - message = "Hello!";

void means that the func does not return a value

Running flutter pub add adds the package to pubspec.yaml and downloads it.

MVVM is an architectural pattern used in client apps that separates your app into three layers:

Model: Handles data operations.
View: Displays the UI.
ViewModel: Manages state and connects the two.
    - ChangeNotifier class to notify UI when data changes
    - To use ChangeNotifier, extend it in your state management class to gain access 
      to the notifyListeners() method, which triggers UI rebuilds when called.

ListenableBuilder is a widget that can "listen" to a ChangeNotifier, and automatically rebuilds when it's provided ChangeNotifier calls notifyListeners().

ValueNotifier is a simple ChangeNotifier that wraps a single value and notifies listeners on change.

Silvers: special widgets that can take advantage of Flutter's powerful and composable scrolling system
    - create sophisticated scroll effects, including   collapsible headers, search integration, and custom scroll behaviors

How do you use a regular widget inside a CustomScrollView's slivers list?
    Wrap it in a SliverToBoxAdapter or    SliverFillRemaining.
        These adapters convert regular widgets into slivers so they can be used in sliver contexts.

